WEBVTT

00:01.007 --> 00:02.967
<b>YEAR OF 1335</b>

00:03.127 --> 00:07.047
<b>DEEP IN THE MOUNTAINS OF SUWA</b>

00:14.437 --> 00:15.477
<b>Take this!</b>

00:15.557 --> 00:16.557
<b>Not a chance!</b>

00:18.767 --> 00:22.687
<b>Such incredible spirit!
It doesn't even feel like training.</b>

00:22.777 --> 00:25.947
<b>Lord Tokiyuki. Do you recognize
anyone among them?</b>

00:29.327 --> 00:32.037
<b>I've never seen any of them
at Suwa Grand Shrine.</b>

00:33.157 --> 00:35.827
<b>They are all surviving retainers
of the Hojo clan.</b>

00:37.377 --> 00:40.917
<b>We secretly took them in
whenever they fled to Shinano.</b>

00:40.997 --> 00:43.297
<b>There are now over a hundred of them.</b>

00:44.087 --> 00:49.507
<b>These men will serve as your personal army
in the coming great battle.</b>

00:50.597 --> 00:54.887
<b>To keep your survival a secret,
we've kept you hidden.</b>

00:54.977 --> 00:58.267
<b>None of them know what you look like.</b>

00:58.357 --> 01:02.227
<b>When the time comes,
reveal your identity to them yourself.</b>

01:02.317 --> 01:05.567
<b>Their spirits will soar beyond measure.</b>

01:07.737 --> 01:10.487
<b>I would love to declare
that we've secured the victory, but…</b>

01:10.577 --> 01:12.657
<b><i>I have nothing but respect for him.</i></b>

01:12.737 --> 01:15.367
<b><i>He's always pestering me</i>
<i>as though he has nothing better to do.</i></b>

01:16.037 --> 01:19.327
<b><i>Yet behind the scenes,</i>
<i>he's been preparing everything.</i></b>

01:20.667 --> 01:21.667
<b>Now then.</b>

01:23.417 --> 01:27.967
<b>There are several individuals
I should like to introduce to you.</b>

01:29.467 --> 01:31.927
<b>These are the Three Great Generals
of the Suwa Sect,</b>

01:32.007 --> 01:34.387
<b>the retainers who serve directly under me.</b>

01:35.017 --> 01:38.807
<b>They shall join us in the battles to come.</b>

01:38.897 --> 01:40.107
<b>The battles to come?</b>

01:40.767 --> 01:44.227
<b>That provincial official is
preparing a full-scale invasion.</b>

01:44.317 --> 01:47.107
<b>We've also received reports
that he's been acting differently.</b>

01:47.857 --> 01:51.027
<b>Let us rescue our allies
throughout the land</b>

01:51.117 --> 01:53.237
<b>while amassing our strength
for the great battle!</b>

02:13.177 --> 02:18.517
<b>THE ELUSIVE SAMURAI</b>

03:26.747 --> 03:29.757
<b>My trusted Three Great Generals!</b>

03:29.837 --> 03:34.547
<b>I have a most astonishing
announcement for you!</b>

03:36.597 --> 03:41.807
<b>This Chojumaru, who has been serving
at Suwa Grand Shrine since last year,</b>

03:41.887 --> 03:46.477
<b>is actually Lord Tokiyuki Hojo,
heir to the Hojo clan!</b>

03:47.357 --> 03:48.397
<b>I see.</b>

03:48.477 --> 03:50.067
<b>That's it?</b>

03:50.147 --> 03:53.907
<b>Surely you can do better than that!</b>

03:53.987 --> 03:58.577
<b>I was looking forward
to seeing the shock on your faces!</b>

03:59.657 --> 04:01.997
<b>Above all else, we are
your direct retainers, Lord Yorishige.</b>

04:02.077 --> 04:03.707
<b>GREAT GENERAL OF THE RIGHT,
SUWA SECT YORINAO NEZU</b>

04:03.787 --> 04:06.837
<b>If you have chosen to rally
behind the heir of the Hojo clan,</b>

04:06.917 --> 04:09.247
<b>then we shall simply follow your lead.</b>

04:11.167 --> 04:13.337
<b>That's how it is, Young Lord.</b>

04:13.427 --> 04:15.757
<b>Please forgive me for having you pour
my sake without knowing who you were.</b>

04:15.837 --> 04:17.467
<b>GREAT GENERAL OF THE LEFT,
SUWA SECT SHIGENOBU MOCHIZUKI</b>

04:18.717 --> 04:21.927
<b>If we treat you any differently,
we'll only put you in more danger.</b>

04:22.477 --> 04:26.687
<b>Until the day your identity is revealed,
you will remain Chojumaru.</b>

04:26.767 --> 04:30.397
<b>We shall treat you just as we always have
in front of others.</b>

04:31.397 --> 04:32.817
<b>Is that acceptable?</b>

04:32.897 --> 04:34.817
<b>GREAT GENERAL OF THE CENTER,
SUWA SECT YUKIYASU UNNO</b>

04:38.867 --> 04:41.077
<b>Myojin is pouting again.</b>

04:41.617 --> 04:44.407
<b>Mochizuki, give him something sweet.</b>

04:44.497 --> 04:46.287
<b>Lord Yorishige, here you are.</b>

04:46.377 --> 04:48.207
<b>-It's delicious.
-Really?</b>

04:48.287 --> 04:50.917
<b><i>They keep a respectful distance from me.</i></b>

04:51.417 --> 04:56.297
<b><i>They're warriors loyal not to the Hojo,</i>
<i>but to Mr. Yorishige.</i></b>

04:56.887 --> 04:59.557
<b><i>They devote their lives</i>
<i>to Suwa Myojin and for Shinano.</i></b>

05:00.717 --> 05:04.557
<b><i>I could feel the bond they forged</i>
<i>through years of mutual trust.</i></b>

05:04.637 --> 05:07.227
<b>PROVINCIAL OFFICIAL'S RESIDENCE</b>

05:09.187 --> 05:12.777
<b>Mercy! Please… spare my wife!</b>

05:16.147 --> 05:22.237
<b>The magistrate has been raising an army
for a rebellion! That's all I know.</b>

05:28.127 --> 05:29.497
<b>Dear!</b>

05:33.507 --> 05:39.927
<b>In winter, slaying is supreme.
Needless to say, slaying rebels.</b>

05:40.007 --> 05:43.347
<b>You truly are an excellent teacher.</b>

05:43.427 --> 05:47.477
<b>My archery has improved
quite a bit, don't you think?</b>

05:47.557 --> 05:48.557
<b>Indeed.</b>

05:48.647 --> 05:50.937
<b>We tortured these peasants
until they confessed,</b>

05:51.017 --> 05:54.527
<b>yet many still oppose me in secret.</b>

05:54.607 --> 05:58.737
<b>I have governed them
with such benevolence, though.</b>

05:58.817 --> 06:01.947
<b>I have obtained an imperial command
from the emperor.</b>

06:02.027 --> 06:05.697
<b>This time, we'll slaughter
every last one of those rebels!</b>

06:09.497 --> 06:12.337
<b>His zeal and cruelty have intensified.</b>

06:12.417 --> 06:17.217
<b>He returned a changed man
after fleeing back to Kyo.</b>

06:17.967 --> 06:20.087
<b>And what of his skill with the bow?</b>

06:20.177 --> 06:24.847
<b>He's improved, but it's still little more
than a noble's pastime.</b>

06:24.927 --> 06:28.307
<b>Just because he can shoot down
defenseless peasants</b>

06:28.387 --> 06:30.847
<b>doesn't mean he'll be any use
on the battlefield.</b>

06:30.937 --> 06:31.937
<b>OFFICIAL</b>

06:32.017 --> 06:34.687
<b><i>Yet he carries himself</i>
<i>with a strange confidence.</i></b>

06:34.777 --> 06:38.487
<b><i>Could he truly intend to lead</i>
<i>from the front himself?</i></b>

06:39.697 --> 06:45.537
<b><i>March, 1335. The flames of conflict</i>
<i>spread across northern Shinano.</i></b>

06:46.157 --> 06:49.457
<b><i>In response, Emperor Godaigo issued</i>
<i>an imperial command</i></b>

06:49.537 --> 06:53.627
<b><i>calling for a simultaneous assault</i>
<i>on pro-Hojo forces throughout the land.</i></b>

06:54.627 --> 06:57.337
<b><i>Within northern Shinano,</i>
<i>Tokoiwa was positioned in the north,</i></b>

06:58.167 --> 07:03.717
<b><i>Hoshina and Shinomiya in the center,</i>
<i>and Tomomitsu Inukai in the south.</i></b>

07:05.007 --> 07:08.017
<b><i>With these three resistance forces</i>
<i>as their primary targets,</i></b>

07:08.097 --> 07:10.807
<b><i>the allied armies of</i>
<i>the provincial official and the governor</i></b>

07:10.887 --> 07:12.767
<b><i>launched a simultaneous offensive.</i></b>

07:13.687 --> 07:16.897
<b><i>Four months remained</i>
<i>until Tokiyuki's uprising.</i></b>

07:17.477 --> 07:20.567
<b><i>This would be the greatest</i>
<i>and final battle before the uprising.</i></b>

07:21.607 --> 07:23.237
<b>The Three Great Generals are
already on their way,</b>

07:23.317 --> 07:28.947
<b>each leading a small force of
elite warriors as secret reinforcements.</b>

07:29.577 --> 07:31.957
<b>So which one are we joining?</b>

07:32.667 --> 07:38.587
<b>None of them. The Elusive Warriors'
mission this time is… messenger duty.</b>

07:38.667 --> 07:39.717
<b>Messenger duty?</b>

07:39.797 --> 07:44.597
<b>You will ride from one battlefield
to the next, carrying reports and orders.</b>

07:45.467 --> 07:48.807
<b>This campaign spans multiple battlefields
over a vast area.</b>

07:48.887 --> 07:52.937
<b>To ensure that every battlefield
receives vital information,</b>

07:53.017 --> 07:56.317
<b>we need messengers
who can never be captured.</b>

07:56.897 --> 07:59.227
<b>We mustn't get caught.</b>

07:59.897 --> 08:01.647
<b>What a difficult mission.</b>

08:02.647 --> 08:07.577
<b>Our objective is the same as before:
to keep our allies' losses to a minimum.</b>

08:08.197 --> 08:09.787
<b>Travel from one battlefield to the next,</b>

08:09.867 --> 08:13.457
<b>and take the opportunity to learn more
about my most trusted retainers.</b>

08:13.537 --> 08:15.787
<b>Your first destination
is the southern part of northern Shinano.</b>

08:15.877 --> 08:19.207
<b>There, Inukai and Unno await
at Fukashi Fort.</b>

08:19.297 --> 08:21.127
<b>They will brief you on the plan.</b>

08:21.797 --> 08:24.377
<b>SOUTHERN FRONT
FUCHU SHINANO, FUKASHI FORT</b>

08:30.307 --> 08:31.767
<b>Mr. Messenger from Suwa Grand Shrine?</b>

08:31.847 --> 08:33.097
<b>FUKASHI MAGISTRATE
TOMOMITSU INUKAI</b>

08:33.187 --> 08:36.307
<b>Oh, so you're that kid
I've heard so much about.</b>

08:36.397 --> 08:39.527
<b>What? People are talking about me?</b>

08:39.607 --> 08:42.607
<b>Aye! They say there's a child
at Suwa Grand Shrine</b>

08:42.687 --> 08:44.567
<b>who's the finest escape artist
in the land.</b>

08:44.657 --> 08:48.277
<b>A naked little freak running all over
the battlefield like he's in heat.</b>

08:48.367 --> 08:49.367
<b>Exaggeration!</b>

08:49.447 --> 08:52.247
<b>Nah, that's not much of an exaggeration</b>

08:52.327 --> 08:54.707
<b>How is the battle going?</b>

08:54.787 --> 08:57.917
<b>Mr. Yorishige told us not to overextend
ourselves, and to fall back if necessary.</b>

08:57.997 --> 08:59.547
<b>The thing is…</b>

09:00.917 --> 09:05.377
<b>Lord Unno's reinforcements are
few in number, yet unbelievably strong.</b>

09:05.467 --> 09:08.757
<b>They haven't even let the Ogasawara army
get anywhere near this fort.</b>

09:11.217 --> 09:15.057
<b>Mr. Unno… He's so cool.</b>

09:15.137 --> 09:16.397
<b>What's he like?</b>

09:16.477 --> 09:18.767
<b>He's the finest general in the Suwa Sect.</b>

09:18.857 --> 09:23.487
<b>His exploits are beyond counting.
He is always composed and calm.</b>

09:23.567 --> 09:26.657
<b>Even without his armor, he looks cool.</b>

09:27.607 --> 09:30.867
<b>The shrine maidens who are
into older men adore him too.</b>

09:30.947 --> 09:34.787
<b>He's kind to everyone, and so thoughtful.
That's what makes him even cooler.</b>

09:35.367 --> 09:39.247
<b>But whenever I tell that to the grown-ups,
they just laugh.</b>

09:39.327 --> 09:40.417
<b>Why?</b>

09:40.497 --> 09:45.717
<b>They always say, "You still don't know
what truly makes him so cool."</b>

09:48.297 --> 09:49.467
<b>Chojumaru.</b>

09:50.297 --> 09:53.807
<b>Tell them this fort won't fall
any time soon.</b>

09:53.887 --> 09:56.727
<b>Not as long as I, Yukiyasu Unno, am here!</b>

09:56.807 --> 09:59.607
<b><i>So cool!</i></b>

10:01.727 --> 10:04.317
<b>-The north gate has been breached!
-What?</b>

10:04.897 --> 10:07.527
<b>Sadamune… He's impressive as ever.</b>

10:07.607 --> 10:10.197
<b>The force we just drove back
was only a diversion.</b>

10:10.277 --> 10:14.907
<b>They drew our attention south
while sending troops around to the north.</b>

10:16.867 --> 10:19.327
<b>Mr. Unno! Um…</b>

10:19.997 --> 10:21.457
<b>Chojumaru.</b>

10:22.537 --> 10:24.837
<b>Have you ever slept with a woman?</b>

10:24.917 --> 10:25.917
<b>Huh?</b>

10:26.007 --> 10:32.347
<b>As if! We are only ten.
Well, someday we'll be like you, Mr. Unno.</b>

10:32.427 --> 10:34.137
<b>-Neither have I.
-What?</b>

10:35.517 --> 10:36.887
<b>I never have.</b>

10:40.727 --> 10:43.687
<b>-I'm completely helpless around women.
<i>-</i>Wha…</b>

10:43.767 --> 10:46.237
<b>Just having a woman speak to me
gets my heart racing.</b>

10:46.317 --> 10:48.987
<b><i>-What?</i>
-When I'm surrounded by shrine maidens,</b>

10:49.067 --> 10:51.947
<b>I get so flustered
I feel like I'm on fire.</b>

10:52.027 --> 10:54.907
<b><i>Why is he suddenly talking about this?</i></b>

10:57.827 --> 11:03.247
<b>I channel every bit of that passion
into serving Suwa Myojin.</b>

11:04.957 --> 11:07.547
<b>Every drop of blood that boils
for a woman,</b>

11:07.627 --> 11:10.797
<b>I pour into my muscles
and my fighting spirit.</b>

11:12.337 --> 11:14.097
<b>It boils, I channel it.</b>

11:14.717 --> 11:19.347
<b>I channel it, I forge myself.
I hone myself, decade after decade.</b>

11:20.637 --> 11:23.727
<b>A Kamakura warrior who remains a virgin
until the age of 30…</b>

11:35.237 --> 11:36.737
<b>becomes a lord of carnage.</b>

11:37.947 --> 11:40.247
<b><i>So cool!</i></b>

11:44.627 --> 11:46.457
<b>UNLOCK THE SECRET
OF THE KAMAKURA WARRIORS</b>

11:46.547 --> 11:51.757
<b><i>Many combat athletes abstain from romance</i>
<i>for a considerable time before a match.</i></b>

11:53.217 --> 11:57.807
<b><i>We spoke with a professor at the Japan</i>
<i>Institute of Imaginary Sports Science.</i></b>

11:57.887 --> 12:01.097
<b><i>He is an expert on how abstinence</i>
<i>affects athletic performance.</i></b>

12:01.187 --> 12:02.977
<b>DEPARTMENT OF ABSTINENCE STUDIES
PROF. KOICHI OSAWA</b>

12:03.057 --> 12:05.807
<b><i>One theory suggests that abstaining</i>
<i>from romance before competition</i></b>

12:05.897 --> 12:10.857
<b><i>increases testosterone</i>
<i>and noradrenaline levels.</i></b>

12:10.937 --> 12:15.817
<b><i>The rise in testosterone caused by</i>
<i>abstinence also increases noradrenaline.</i></b>

12:15.907 --> 12:18.197
<b><i>Energy is conserved for battle</i></b>

12:18.287 --> 12:21.537
<b><i>and transformed</i>
<i>into explosive primal strength.</i></b>

12:22.247 --> 12:26.877
<b><i>If the kamakura warriors, who were</i>
<i>even more hot-blooded than people today,</i></b>

12:26.957 --> 12:30.457
<b><i>spent a lifetime denying those desires</i>
<i>and devoted all that energy to battle…</i></b>

12:31.337 --> 12:35.717
<b><i>they might become lords of carnage</i>
<i>beyond anything we can imagine.</i></b>

12:44.267 --> 12:47.767
<b>He cut down ten men before
the pieces of paper even hit the ground.</b>

12:48.517 --> 12:51.187
<b><i>I still don't really understand</i>
<i>the desire between men and women,</i></b>

12:51.277 --> 12:54.447
<b><i>but I've always been told</i>
<i>it can't be suppressed.</i></b>

12:55.027 --> 12:59.407
<b><i>Yet he's endured them for decades</i>
<i>through loyalty and faith.</i></b>

12:59.487 --> 13:03.907
<b><i>And unlike a monk, he hasn't cast those</i>
<i>earthly desires aside or forgotten them.</i></b>

13:03.997 --> 13:07.167
<b><i>He's kept them boiling inside him</i>
<i>all this time.</i></b>

13:07.747 --> 13:11.087
<b><i>As expected of Mr. Yorishige's retainers.</i></b>

13:11.167 --> 13:13.667
<b><i>Only loyalty of that caliber</i>
<i>could make such a thing possible.</i></b>

13:16.757 --> 13:19.557
<b>Now then. We've driven them back
for the moment,</b>

13:19.637 --> 13:22.017
<b>but this battle won't end that easily.</b>

13:22.767 --> 13:26.307
<b>Shizuku, you're aware of the situation
at all three battlefields, correct?</b>

13:26.397 --> 13:27.807
<b>Yes.</b>

13:31.147 --> 13:35.697
<b>The northern battlefield is Ichikawa
versus Mr. Mochizuki and Mr. Tokoiwa.</b>

13:35.777 --> 13:37.867
<b>The central battlefield is
the provincial official</b>

13:37.947 --> 13:39.867
<b>versus Mr. Nezu and the Hoshina’s party.</b>

13:39.947 --> 13:44.077
<b>Here in the south, it's Sadamune
versus Mr. Unno and Mr. Inukai.</b>

13:44.157 --> 13:46.037
<b>ICHIKAWA’S ARMY - TOKOIWA'S ARMY
MOCHIZUKI’S ARMY</b>

13:46.117 --> 13:48.787
<b>Whichever side wins its battle
can reinforce the others.</b>

13:49.287 --> 13:53.337
<b>That means if even one front falls,
the whole campaign could collapse.</b>

13:53.417 --> 13:57.257
<b>So the three battlefields must stay
in contact and work together.</b>

13:59.847 --> 14:01.177
<b>Exactly.</b>

14:02.097 --> 14:05.097
<b>Of the three,
Sadamune's army is the strongest.</b>

14:05.177 --> 14:07.937
<b>If things continue as they are, we can
keep them pinned here for ten days.</b>

14:08.687 --> 14:10.807
<b>Ideally, Ichikawa's army in the north</b>

14:10.897 --> 14:13.067
<b>and the provincial official's army
in the center…</b>

14:13.147 --> 14:14.147
<b>-Let's call it off.
-Okay.</b>

14:14.227 --> 14:16.447
<b>…can be driven into retreat
after suffering heavy losses.</b>

14:17.027 --> 14:19.407
<b>Carry that message
to the northern and central fronts.</b>

14:19.487 --> 14:23.447
<b>See how things stand there,
then act as the situation demands.</b>

14:23.537 --> 14:27.327
<b>Understood, Mr. Unno.
We'll be on our way at once.</b>

14:29.207 --> 14:33.337
<b>Wait! There are still enemies
near the fort.</b>

14:33.417 --> 14:35.507
<b>You should wait until nightfall
before heading out.</b>

14:35.587 --> 14:38.257
<b>If we wait until nightfall,
the information will arrive too late.</b>

14:38.337 --> 14:41.387
<b>We have to get it to our allies
as quickly as possible.</b>

14:42.047 --> 14:44.097
<b>Don't worry. We won't get caught.</b>

14:44.677 --> 14:46.597
<b>Come on, everyone. Let's run!</b>

14:47.227 --> 14:48.347
<b>All right.</b>

14:57.437 --> 15:01.367
<b>Is that… Enemy messengers! Kill them!</b>

15:07.827 --> 15:09.207
<b>Keep going straight.</b>

15:09.827 --> 15:12.667
<b>I'll circle around and draw them away.</b>

15:24.717 --> 15:25.717
<b>Get him!</b>

15:33.557 --> 15:35.437
<b>Damn brat!</b>

15:35.517 --> 15:39.737
<b>Hasn't his riding improved a lot
over the past year?</b>

15:39.817 --> 15:42.027
<b>I taught him how to flee on horseback.</b>

15:42.107 --> 15:46.197
<b>Once he realized it'd help him escape,
he practiced with all his heart.</b>

15:46.287 --> 15:48.697
<b>He's never looked more alive.</b>

15:48.787 --> 15:53.127
<b>So that's the famed master of escape.
He's brimming with the will to survive.</b>

15:54.077 --> 15:55.877
<b>We should learn from him!</b>

15:57.497 --> 16:01.427
<b><i>The Elusive Samurai indeed.</i>
<i>He's been a good influence on us.</i></b>

16:01.927 --> 16:03.587
<b><i>Now then…</i></b>

16:08.717 --> 16:14.147
<b>I want to have female retainers
rallying around me like that!</b>

16:20.397 --> 16:24.817
<b>CENTRAL FRONT
KAWANAKAJIMA</b>

16:25.737 --> 16:29.037
<b>Mr. Messenger! It's been a while.
Has it really been a year?</b>

16:29.117 --> 16:31.867
<b>Mr. Hoshina.
I'm so glad to see you're safe.</b>

16:35.247 --> 16:37.627
<b>Here to help? Good lad, Kojiro!</b>

16:38.587 --> 16:42.377
<b>Knock it off, you old geezers!
I'm here on messenger duty!</b>

16:47.097 --> 16:49.887
<b>Mr. Hoshina, could you tell us
how the battle is progressing?</b>

16:49.967 --> 16:52.727
<b>It's a stalemate wherever you look.</b>

16:52.807 --> 16:55.147
<b>The battlefield's
much larger than last time.</b>

16:55.847 --> 16:59.527
<b>It's hard to predict where the provincial
official's army will strike next.</b>

16:59.607 --> 17:04.357
<b>But at times like this, there's no one
more dependable than Mr. Nezu.</b>

17:28.597 --> 17:29.887
<b>The provincial official's right flank</b>

17:29.967 --> 17:31.927
<b>looks like a massive force
from the ground.</b>

17:32.017 --> 17:35.767
<b>But from above, it's nothing more than
a thin line spread wide to intimidate us.</b>

17:35.847 --> 17:37.347
<b>Charge through and scatter them.</b>

17:37.437 --> 17:38.437
<b>Yes, sir.</b>

17:39.267 --> 17:42.317
<b>The provincial official's left flank
is the real threat.</b>

17:42.397 --> 17:45.607
<b>They're concealed in the forest,
waiting to cross the Sai River.</b>

17:45.697 --> 17:48.777
<b>-Signal Shinomiya with drums and smoke.
-Yes, sir.</b>

17:53.907 --> 17:55.367
<b>-Move out.
-Yes, sir!</b>

17:58.747 --> 18:01.297
<b>He reads the battlefield
through his hawks.</b>

18:02.167 --> 18:06.217
<b>Surveying vast battlefields
is the Nezu clan's specialty.</b>

18:06.927 --> 18:10.597
<b>Oh, right. Kojiro. You're a member
of the Nezu clan too.</b>

18:10.677 --> 18:12.097
<b>Chojumaru.</b>

18:13.347 --> 18:15.427
<b>How goes the southern front?</b>

18:17.977 --> 18:19.807
<b>So the south can hold
for another ten days.</b>

18:20.477 --> 18:23.817
<b>In that case, our greatest concern
remains the northern front.</b>

18:24.647 --> 18:27.027
<b>Ichikawa commands a formidable force.</b>

18:27.107 --> 18:29.697
<b>Even with Mochizuki reinforcing them,</b>

18:29.777 --> 18:32.487
<b>Tokoiwa is still
the weakest of our allies.</b>

18:33.407 --> 18:35.997
<b>EZ WIN</b>

18:36.077 --> 18:39.877
<b>If the north falls before
we weaken the provincial official's army,</b>

18:39.957 --> 18:45.007
<b>both forces will converge
on the central front.</b>

18:45.087 --> 18:46.627
<b>TOKOIWA - MOCHIZUKI - ICHIKAWA</b>

18:52.507 --> 18:58.307
<b><i>Ayako is Mr. Mochizuki's daughter.</i>
<i>She must be worried about her father too.</i></b>

19:00.187 --> 19:01.187
<b>Understood.</b>

19:02.057 --> 19:04.937
<b>I'll find out how much longer
the northern front can hold.</b>

19:05.027 --> 19:06.817
<b>-What?
-Now?</b>

19:06.897 --> 19:09.317
<b>You've already been riding for a full day.</b>

19:09.397 --> 19:11.237
<b>Just give me a fresh horse.</b>

19:11.317 --> 19:15.737
<b>I'm actually having fun
slipping past the enemy patrols.</b>

19:15.827 --> 19:19.037
<b>-Right, everyone?
-You're the only one, My Lord.</b>

19:19.117 --> 19:20.537
<b>YOU'RE COMING WITH ME, RIGHT?
DRAINED</b>

19:20.617 --> 19:24.377
<b>Kojiro, Ayako, Fubuki. Come with me.</b>

19:24.457 --> 19:25.497
<b>Yes!</b>

19:26.627 --> 19:30.467
<b>Shizuku, Genba. Get some rest
while you analyze the battle.</b>

19:30.547 --> 19:31.547
<b>Understood.</b>

19:35.007 --> 19:37.767
<b>Never change, Mr. Messenger.</b>

19:37.847 --> 19:38.847
<b>Huh?</b>

19:45.517 --> 19:47.187
<b>Leaving already, Kojiro?</b>

19:47.277 --> 19:50.277
<b>I'll be back!
You're as much of a pain as ever.</b>

19:51.907 --> 19:55.697
<b>We'll line up plenty of ears and noses
to mark your way back.</b>

19:55.777 --> 19:56.787
<b>No, thank you!</b>

19:56.867 --> 19:57.867
<b>Kojiro.</b>

20:03.787 --> 20:06.457
<b>From today on, cover your face
whenever you take the field.</b>

20:09.337 --> 20:14.137
<b>Do your duty well.
For Lord Yorishige. For our Nezu clan.</b>

20:22.017 --> 20:23.017
<b>Yes.</b>

20:37.367 --> 20:40.537
<b>Something felt strange between those two.</b>

20:40.617 --> 20:42.537
<b>I don't know all the details,</b>

20:42.617 --> 20:45.537
<b>but it sounds like his family situation
is a little complicated.</b>

20:45.627 --> 20:46.627
<b>What?</b>

20:47.917 --> 20:50.587
<b>It's nothing to worry about.</b>

20:50.667 --> 20:56.007
<b>No, I mean… that headband suits you.
Everyone goes through a phase like that.</b>

20:56.087 --> 20:57.097
<b>Shut up!</b>

21:05.977 --> 21:09.437
<b>We've entered Tokoiwa territory!
Let's hurry to Kitajo Fort!</b>

21:22.697 --> 21:24.367
<b>NORTHERN FRONT
TOKOIWA'S STRONGHOLD KITAJO FORT</b>

21:24.457 --> 21:26.077
<b>The fort.</b>

21:31.127 --> 21:32.257
<b>Ayako!</b>

21:32.337 --> 21:33.877
<b>Father.</b>

21:36.087 --> 21:40.467
<b>I took a quick look around.
Ichikawa's army is virtually untouched.</b>

21:41.387 --> 21:42.887
<b>MOCHIZUKI’S ARMY
TOKOIWA’S ARMY 170</b>

21:42.977 --> 21:43.977
<b>ICHIKAWA’S ARMY 300</b>

21:44.057 --> 21:47.767
<b><i>If Ichikawa's army joins forces</i>
<i>with the Provincial Official's army</i></b>

21:47.857 --> 21:50.517
<b><i>in the center at full strength,</i>
<i>the balance will be shattered.</i></b>

21:51.187 --> 21:52.187
<b>This can't be.</b>

22:00.277 --> 22:03.497
<b><i>By tomorrow, our defeat will be certain!</i></b>

23:39.007 --> 23:39.877
<b>-Let's go!
-Let's go!</b>
